# Include repo-committed agent skills in the sdist. The files live outside
# src/codeprobe/ so they cannot be declared in [tool.setuptools.package-data];
# this MANIFEST.in + `include-package-data = true` in pyproject.toml is the
# equivalent mechanism for setuptools builds. See PRD §7 (paired-skills).
#
# Listed one by one, not `recursive-include .claude/skills SKILL.md`: that
# directory is a shared namespace, and a recursive rule would sweep whatever
# machine-local agent skills the person running `python -m build` happens to
# have into a public sdist.
include .claude/skills/codeprobe-calibrate/SKILL.md
include .claude/skills/codeprobe-check-infra/SKILL.md
include .claude/skills/codeprobe-interpret/SKILL.md
include .claude/skills/codeprobe-mine/SKILL.md
include .claude/skills/codeprobe-run/SKILL.md
